Chapter: RealLiteralProbe

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Scratch probe for COMPILER-37. Separates the PARSE from the PRINT: each
 row shows the literal, its value through real-to-int (the parsed bits as
 an integer), and its value through show (the printer). If real-to-int is
 right and show is wrong, the defect is in the formatter and not the
 parser, and the reverse tells the opposite story.

 Rows climb the digit count so the first wrong row names the threshold.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("d09        : " & show (real-to-int 123456789.0) & "  show=" & show 123456789.0)
    print-line-uni ("d15        : " & show (real-to-int 123456789012345.0) & "  show=" & show 123456789012345.0)
    print-line-uni ("d16        : " & show (real-to-int 1234567890123456.0) & "  show=" & show 1234567890123456.0)
    print-line-uni ("d17        : " & show (real-to-int 12345678901234567.0) & "  show=" & show 12345678901234567.0)
    print-line-uni ("d18        : " & show (real-to-int 123456789012345678.0) & "  show=" & show 123456789012345678.0)
    print-line-uni ("half       : " & show (real-to-int 0.5) & "  show=" & show 0.5)
    print-line-uni ("onepoint5  : " & show (real-to-int 1.5) & "  show=" & show 1.5)
  end

